        rounded: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
        padding: "16px 24px"
  link-on-light:
    description: "DESIGN.md component token group"
    when: ["as documented in rationale.components and getdesign analysis"]
    when_not: ["decorative misuse outside brand patterns"]
    variants: [default]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.canvas}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.body-md}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
        padding: "0px"
  footer-light:
    description: "DESIGN.md component token group"
    when: ["as documented in rationale.components and getdesign analysis"]
    when_not: ["decorative misuse outside brand patterns"]
    variants: [default]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.canvas}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.ink-mute}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.caption}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
        padding: "64px 24px"

rationale:
  overview: |
    Stripe's design language opens with the gradient mesh. A wide horizontal band of pastel cream, sherbet orange, lavender, electric indigo, and ruby pink occupies the upper third of nearly every marketing page — the brand's instantly-recognizable atmospheric backdrop. Type and product UI mockups float above it on `{tokens.color.canvas}` (white), with the gradient acting as both decoration and visual anchor. The lower portion of the page returns to white, with feature explanations on `{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` (a barely-tinted cool off-white) and dashboard product mockups composited as faux IDE/console panels in deep navy.
    
    The color system has two primary roles. **Indigo** (`{tokens.color.primary}` — `#533afd`) is the brand's signature CTA color, used sparingly: one filled pill per band. **Deep navy** (`{tokens.color.ink}` — `#0d253d`) is the universal body text color and the fill of dashboard mockups, the featured pricing tier, and the dark-app surfaces on the dashboard track. Ruby (`{tokens.color.ruby}`) and magenta (`{tokens.color.magenta}`) appear inside the gradient mesh and as accent dots in product UI mockups; they are not used as button colors.
    
    Typography is built around **Sohne** at weight 300 with negative letter-spacing — the brand's editorial-density display signature. Display sizes (32–56px) use -1.4px to -0.64px tracking; body sizes use 0; tabular caption sizes (where money and numerics matter) use the OpenType `tnum` feature plus a tightening -0.36 to -0.42px tracking. The `ss01` stylistic set is enabled across all roles.
    
    **Key Characteristics:**
    - Gradient-mesh backdrop on every marketing hero — cream/orange/lavender/indigo/ruby horizontally washed across the upper third of the page.
    - Single-indigo CTA hierarchy: filled `{tokens.color.primary}` pill is the only filled button on marketing surfaces.
    - Sohne thin (weight 300) display tier with negative tracking from -1.4px to -0.2px depending on size.
    - Tabular-figure body type (`tnum`) for any cell containing money or numerics — the brand's quiet financial-data signal.
    - Dark-app dashboard track: deep navy product UI mockups sit composited above the white canvas, frequently with rendered code or dashboard tables inside.
    - Pill-shaped buttons (`{tokens.radius.pill}` 9999px) with tight `8px 16px` padding — short, decisive, transactional.
    - Cream-band feature cards (`{tokens.color.canvas-cream}`) introduce a warm interlude between blue/white sections without breaking the brand's chromatic logic.
  colors: |
    > **Source pages:** home (`/`), `/payments`, `/pricing`, `dashboard.stripe.com/register/payments`.
    
    ### Brand & Accent
    - **Indigo** (`{tokens.color.primary}` — `#533afd`): The brand's signature CTA color. Filled-pill button, link emphasis, gradient anchor.
    - **Indigo Deep** (`{tokens.color.primary-deep}` — `#4434d4`): A deeper indigo used in gradient mid-stops and as the press-state warmer alternative.
    - **Indigo Press** (`{tokens.color.primary-press}` — `#2e2b8c`): Pressed-state lift of the primary.
    - **Indigo Soft** (`{tokens.color.primary-soft}` — `#665efd`): A lighter indigo used in product-UI accents and chart highlights.
    - **Indigo Subdued** (`{tokens.color.primary-bg-subdued-hover}` — `#b9b9f9`): Pale indigo fill used as soft tag background.
    - **Brand Dark 900** (`{tokens.color.brand-dark-900}` — `#1c1e54`): The deep navy used on the featured pricing tier and dashboard chrome.
    - **Ruby** (`{tokens.color.ruby}` — `#ea2261`): Gradient accent and chart highlight; never a button.
    - **Magenta** (`{tokens.color.magenta}` — `#f96bee`): Brighter pink stop in gradient meshes.
    - **Lemon** (`{tokens.color.lemon}` — `#9b6829`): Warm sherbet stop in gradient backdrops.
    
    ### Surface
    - **Canvas** (`{tokens.color.canvas}` — `#ffffff`): Default page background.
    - **Canvas Soft** (`{tokens.color.canvas-soft}` — `#f6f9fc`): Cool-tinted off-white used on feature bands beneath the gradient hero.
    - **Canvas Cream** (`{tokens.color.canvas-cream}` — `#f5e9d4`): Warm cream used as a feature-band fill — the brand's chromatic interlude.
    - **Hairline** (`{tokens.color.hairline}` — `#e3e8ee`): 1px borders on cards and tables.
    - **Hairline Input** (`{tokens.color.hairline-input}` — `#a8c3de`): Slightly cooler hairline used on form inputs.
    
    ### Text
    - **Ink** (`{tokens.color.ink}` — `#0d253d`): Default body text color across the brand. Deep navy, never pure black.
    - **Ink Secondary** (`{tokens.color.ink-secondary}` — `#273951`): Secondary text on white.
    - **Ink Mute** (`{tokens.color.ink-mute}` — `#64748d`): Helper text, captions, table labels.
    - **Ink Mute 2** (`{tokens.color.ink-mute-2}` — `#61718a`): Near-equivalent to ink-mute used in nav.
    - **On Primary** (`{tokens.color.on-primary}` — `#ffffff`): Text on indigo / dark-navy surfaces.
    
    ### Semantic
    The brand does not use a separate semantic color palette in the marketing system — error / success states live in dashboard-product UI specifically.
  typography: |
    ### Font Family
    
    The display and UI tier is **Sohne** (proprietary, licensed from Klim Type Foundry) at weights 300 (thin) and 400 (regular). The variable font (`sohne-var`) is loaded with `font-feature-settings: "ss01"` enabled globally — the stylistic set substitutes a single-story `a` and other character variants that are part of the brand's typographic signature.
    
    When Sohne is unavailable, fall back to **SF Pro Display** at thin weights, then system-ui. For maximum brand fidelity, **Inter** (open-source) at weight 300 with `font-feature-settings: "ss01"` and `letter-spacing: -1.4px` on display sizes approximates the rhythm closely.
    
    ### Hierarchy
    
    | Token | Size | Weight | Line Height | Letter Spacing | Use |
    |---|---|---|---|---|---|
    | `{tokens.typography.display-xxl}` | 56px | 300 | 1.03 | -1.4px | Hero headline |
    | `{tokens.typography.display-xl}` | 48px | 300 | 1.15 | -0.96px | Section opener |
    | `{tokens.typography.display-lg}` | 32px | 300 | 1.1 | -0.64px | Card title / sub-section |
    | `{tokens.typography.display-md}` | 26px | 300 | 1.12 | -0.26px | Compact card title |
    | `{tokens.typography.heading-lg}` | 22px | 300 | 1.1 | -0.22px | Pricing tier name |
    | `{tokens.typography.heading-md}` | 20px | 300 | 1.4 | -0.2px | Section sub-heading |
    | `{tokens.typography.heading-sm}` | 18px | 300 | 1.4 | 0 | Mini-section label |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-lg}` | 16px | 300 | 1.4 | 0 | Marketing body lead |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-md}` | 15px | 300 | 1.4 | 0 | Default UI body |
    | `{tokens.typography.body-tabular}` | 14px | 300 | 1.4 | -0.42px | Money / numeric tables (uses `tnum`) |
    | `{tokens.typography.button-md}` | 16px | 400 | 1.0 | 0 | Pill button label |
    | `{tokens.typography.button-sm}` | 14px | 400 | 1.0 | 0 | Compact pill label |
    | `{tokens.typography.caption}` | 13px | 400 | 1.4 | -0.39px | Helper, table labels |
    | `{tokens.typography.micro}` | 11px | 300 | 1.4 | 0 | Fine print |
    | `{tokens.typography.micro-cap}` | 10px | 400 | 1.15 | 0.1px | All-caps eyebrow |
    
    ### Principles
    - **Thin weight is the brand.** Display tiers always render at weight 300. Bumping to 400+ removes the brand's editorial air.
    - **Negative tracking on display.** -1.4px at 56px, scaling proportionally down to -0.2px at 20px. The negative tracking is the brand's typographic signature.
    - **Tabular figures for money.** Any cell rendering currency, transaction amounts, or numeric counts uses `font-feature-settings: "tnum"` plus a tightening tracking. The brand quietly signals its financial DNA through this micro-detail.
    - **`ss01` globally.** Apply `font-feature-settings: "ss01"` to the body element so the stylistic-set substitution is on for every text role.
    
    ### Note on Font Substitutes
    Sohne is proprietary. Use **Inter** (open-source via Google Fonts) at weight 300 with `letter-spacing: -1.4px` and `font-feature-settings: "ss01"` for display tiers — Inter is the closest open-source analogue. For body sizes, Inter at 300 weight with `font-feature-settings: "tnum"` (where applicable) is the canonical substitute. Avoid Helvetica or system-ui defaults — they're heavier than the brand needs.
  layout: |
    ### Spacing System
    - **Base unit**: 8px (with 2 / 4 / 12 sub-tokens for fine work).
    - **Tokens**: `{tokens.spacing.xxs}` 2px · `{tokens.spacing.xs}` 4px · `{tokens.spacing.sm}` 8px · `{tokens.spacing.md}` 12px · `{tokens.spacing.lg}` 16px · `{tokens.spacing.xl}` 24px · `{tokens.spacing.xxl}` 32px · `{tokens.spacing.huge}` 64px.
    - **Section padding**: 64–96px on marketing surfaces; 32–48px on dashboard / product surfaces.
    - **Card internal padding**: 32px on feature cards; 24px on dashboard mockups.
    
    ### Grid & Container
    - Marketing pages center in a ~1200px container with the gradient mesh extending edge-to-edge above.
    - Pricing collapses 4-up → 2-up → 1-up at 1024 / 768 breakpoints.
    - Dashboard product mockups use their own internal grids (12-col tables, 3-col card grids) rendered as static composites.
    
    ### Whitespace Philosophy
    The gradient mesh occupies the upper third of the page; the white canvas below is generously padded. Section gaps tend toward 96px, with content tightening to 32px on dashboard / pricing pages where users compare and act.
  elevation: |
    | Level | Treatment | Use |
    |---|---|---|
    | 0 | Flat | Default surface |
    | 1 | `box-shadow: rgba(0,55,112,0.08) 0 1px 3px` | Card lift on white |
    | 2 | `box-shadow: rgba(0,55,112,0.08) 0 8px 24px, rgba(0,55,112,0.04) 0 2px 6px` | Floating panels, dashboard mockup chrome |
    | 3 | Gradient mesh backdrop | The brand's primary depth medium — atmospheric color rather than literal shadow |
    
    ### Decorative Depth
    The gradient mesh IS the depth system. Implemented as a layered SVG or large background image rather than CSS gradients (the actual mesh has organic blob shapes that aren't CSS-renderable). The mesh provides the brand's signature lift; literal shadows are reserved for product-UI mockups and stay subtle.
  shapes: |
    ### Border Radius Scale
    
    | Token | Value | Use |
    |---|---|---|
    | `{tokens.radius.xs}` | 4px | Hairline tags, table chrome |
    | `{tokens.radius.sm}` | 6px | Form inputs |
    | `{tokens.radius.md}` | 8px | Compact cards, alerts |
    | `{tokens.radius.lg}` | 12px | Pricing cards, feature cards |
    | `{tokens.radius.xl}` | 16px | Dashboard product mockup chrome |
    | `{tokens.radius.pill}` | 9999px | All buttons, tag pills |
    
    ### Photography Geometry
    The brand uses **product UI mockups** more than photography. Dashboard composites render as faux IDE/terminal/dashboard chrome inside `{tokens.radius.lg}` 12px containers with a subtle `box-shadow`. Real photography appears in customer logo strips and the rare case-study card; treated as inset 4:3 with no shadow.
  components: |
    ### Buttons
    
    **`button-primary-pill`** — the dominant CTA system-wide.
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, type `{tokens.typography.button-md}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.sm} {tokens.spacing.lg}` (8px 16px), rounded `{tokens.radius.pill}` 9999px.
    - Pressed state `button-primary-pill-pressed` shifts background to `{tokens.color.primary-press}`.
    
    **`button-secondary`** — outline-style alternative.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.primary}`, 1px solid `{tokens.color.primary}` border, same pill geometry.
    
    **`button-on-dark`** — used on dashboard / dark surfaces.
    - Background `{tokens.color.brand-dark-900}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, same pill geometry.
    
    ### Cards & Containers
    
    **`card-feature-light`** — feature explanation card on white.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.xxl}`, rounded `{tokens.radius.lg}` 12px, 1px `{tokens.color.hairline}` border, optional Level 1 shadow.
    
    **`card-pricing`** — standard pricing tier.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.xxl}`, rounded `{tokens.radius.lg}`, 1px `{tokens.color.hairline}` border. Title `{tokens.typography.heading-lg}`, price `{tokens.typography.display-md}`, body `{tokens.typography.body-md}`, CTA pinned bottom as `button-primary-pill`.
    
    **`card-pricing-featured`** — the inverted dark featured tier.
    - Background `{tokens.color.brand-dark-900}`, text `{tokens.color.on-primary}`, otherwise identical structure to `card-pricing`. The deep-navy fill is the brand's distinctive featured-tier choice.
    
    **`card-cream-band`** — warm interlude card.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas-cream}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.xxl}`, rounded `{tokens.radius.lg}`. Used to break up the indigo / white rhythm with warmth.
    
    **`card-dashboard-mockup`** — composited dashboard / product UI screenshot.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, type `{tokens.typography.body-tabular}` (with `tnum`), padding `{tokens.spacing.xl}` 24px, rounded `{tokens.radius.lg}` 12px, Level 2 shadow. Often contains nested mini-mockups: code preview + dashboard table + chart card.
    
    ### Inputs & Forms
    
    **`text-input`** — standard form field.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink}`, type `{tokens.typography.body-md}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.sm} {tokens.spacing.md}` (8px 12px), rounded `{tokens.radius.sm}` 6px, 1px `{tokens.color.hairline-input}` border.
    - Focus state `text-input-focused`: border swaps to `{tokens.color.primary}`.
    
    ### Navigation
    
    **`nav-bar-on-mesh`** — top nav floating over the gradient hero.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}` (or transparent depending on scroll), text `{tokens.color.ink}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.lg} {tokens.spacing.xl}`. Logo wordmark on the left, primary nav center, sign-in + filled `button-primary-pill` on the right.
    
    ### Pills, Tags, and Chips
    
    **`pill-tag-soft`** — subdued indigo tag.
    - Background `{tokens.color.primary-bg-subdued-hover}`, text `{tokens.color.primary-deep}`, type `{tokens.typography.micro-cap}`, padding `4px 8px`, rounded `{tokens.radius.pill}`.
    
    ### Signature Components
    
    **Gradient Mesh Backdrop** — pastel cream → sherbet orange → lavender → indigo → ruby pink stops blurred horizontally across the upper third of the page. Implemented as SVG or a large background image — not a flat CSS gradient (the real mesh has organic blob shapes).
    
    **Composited Dashboard Mockup** — multi-layer faux-product-UI compositions: an IDE panel on the left, a dashboard table center, a chart card on the right, all rendered at small scale inside `{tokens.radius.lg}` containers with subtle Level 2 shadows. The composite is the brand's most-photographed feature.
    
    **Tabular-Figure Money Type** — every number rendering money, count, or transaction value uses `font-feature-settings: "tnum"`. The brand's quiet signal that it's a financial-infrastructure platform.
    
    **`link-on-light`** — inline links on light surfaces.
    - Text `{tokens.color.primary}` rendered in `{tokens.typography.body-md}`, no underline by default.
    
    **`footer-light`** — site-wide footer.
    - Background `{tokens.color.canvas}`, text `{tokens.color.ink-mute}`, type `{tokens.typography.caption}`, padding `{tokens.spacing.huge} {tokens.spacing.xl}` (64px 24px). Holds 4–6 columns of link groups, social icons, and a small legal row.
  responsive: |
    ### Breakpoints
    
    | Name | Width | Key Changes |
    |---|---|---|
    | Wide | ≥ 1440px | Full gradient mesh edge-to-edge; dashboard composite at full scale |
    | Desktop | 1024–1440px | Default content max-width; pricing 4-up |
    | Tablet | 768–1023px | Pricing 2-up; dashboard composite simplifies to 2 panels |
    | Mobile | < 768px | Pricing 1-up; hamburger nav; display drops 56 → 36px |
    
    ### Touch Targets
    - Pill buttons hit ≥ 40×40px on mobile via padding scaling. On smaller screens, buttons size up to 44×44px to maintain WCAG AAA.
    - Form fields stay at 40px minimum height.
    
    ### Collapsing Strategy
    - Display tiers stair-step 56 → 48 → 32 → 26 → 22px through the breakpoints.
    - Gradient mesh re-tiles on mobile to preserve the wash without disappearing.
    - Dashboard composites simplify to single-panel mockups on mobile; the multi-layer composition only renders at desktop+.
    - Pricing tiers stair-step 4-up → 2-up → 1-up.
    
    ### Image Behavior
    Product UI composites use `srcset` with art-direction crops at major breakpoints. Mobile crops focus on the most actionable inner panel; desktop crops show the full multi-layer composition.
  iteration: |
    1. Focus on ONE component at a time.
    2. Reference component names and tokens directly (`{tokens.color.primary}`, `{button-primary-pill}-pressed`, `{tokens.radius.pill}`).
    3. Run `npx @google/design.md lint DESIGN.md` after edits.
    4. Add new variants as separate entries.
    5. Default body to `{tokens.typography.body-md}` (15px); use `{tokens.typography.body-tabular}` for any money / numeric cell.
    6. Apply `ss01` globally on the body; apply `tnum` per-element on numeric content.
    7. The gradient mesh is non-negotiable on marketing heroes — bare-canvas heroes break the brand.
  dos:
    - "Reserve `{tokens.color.primary}` for filled CTAs and inline link emphasis \u2014 it should appear sparingly, one filled button per band."
    - Apply the gradient mesh to every marketing hero; bare-canvas heroes feel off-brand.
    - Render display tiers at weight 300 with negative letter-spacing — the thin tracking is the typographic signature.
    - "Use `font-feature-settings: \"tnum\"` on every money / numeric cell."
    - "Apply `font-feature-settings: \"ss01\"` globally on the body element."
    - Pair every feature explanation with a composited product UI mockup; the brand's argument is "look at the actual product."
  donts:
    - bump display weight above 300 — at 400 the brand's editorial air collapses.
    - add new accent colors outside the documented gradient stops (cream / orange / lavender / indigo / ruby / magenta).
    - "use the indigo `{tokens.color.primary}` as a body-text color \u2014 it's a CTA and link color, not a type color at body size."
    - "shrink button padding below `8px 16px` \u2014 the tight pill is part of the brand's transactional feel."
    - "render money cells without `tnum` \u2014 it breaks the quiet financial-data signature."
    - replace the pill shape with rounded-rectangles for buttons.

omitted:
  - section: tokens.elevation
    reason: "Depth model lives in rationale.elevation; add shadow tokens as they stabilize"

integrations:
  shadcn:
    enabled: true
    style: new-york            # legacy style; current styles: see SPEC §7.1
    icon_library: lucide
    css_variables: true
    base_color: neutral
    css: app/globals.css
    components_json: ./components.json
    aliases:
      components: "@/components"
      utils: "@/lib/utils"
      ui: "@/components/ui"
      lib: "@/lib"
      hooks: "@/hooks"
    radius: "8px"
    css_vars:
      theme:
        radius: "8px"
      light:
        background: "#ffffff"
        foreground: "#0d253d"
        card: "#ffffff"
        card-foreground: "#0d253d"
        popover: "#ffffff"
        popover-foreground: "#0d253d"
        primary: "#533afd"
        primary-foreground: "#ffffff"
        secondary: "#f4f4f5"
        secondary-foreground: "#0d253d"
        muted: "#f4f4f5"
        muted-foreground: "#0d253d"
        accent: "#f4f4f5"
        accent-foreground: "#0d253d"
        destructive: "#dc2626"
        border: "#e3e8ee"
        input: "#e3e8ee"
        ring: "#533afd"
        sidebar: "#ffffff"
        sidebar-foreground: "#0d253d"
        sidebar-primary: "#533afd"
        sidebar-primary-foreground: "#ffffff"
        sidebar-accent: "#f4f4f5"
        sidebar-accent-foreground: "#0d253d"
        sidebar-border: "#e3e8ee"
        sidebar-ring: "#533afd"
    map_from_tokens:
      background: tokens.color.canvas|tokens.color.surface|tokens.color.background
      foreground: tokens.color.ink|tokens.color.text|tokens.color.foreground
      primary: tokens.color.primary
      primary-foreground: tokens.color.on-primary
      border: tokens.color.hairline|tokens.color.border
      ring: tokens.color.primary-focus|tokens.color.primary

policy:
  if_missing: ask
  hierarchy: [typography, spacing, contrast, color]
  reuse:
    prefer_existing_components: true
  accessibility:
    contrast: AA
    focus_visible: required

constraints:
  always:
    - use semantic tokens from this file; never invent off-brand hex
    - bind every listed component property (backgroundColor, textColor, typography, rounded, padding, size, height, width)
    - read rationale.layout / rationale.elevation / rationale.shapes before inventing chrome
    - when shadcn is enabled, apply integrations.shadcn.css_vars to globals.css
    - prefer catalog components over one-off controls
    - "Reserve `{tokens.color.primary}` for filled CTAs and inline link emphasis \u2014 it should appear sparingly, one filled button per band."
    - Apply the gradient mesh to every marketing hero; bare-canvas heroes feel off-brand.
    - Render display tiers at weight 300 with negative letter-spacing — the thin tracking is the typographic signature.
    - "Use `font-feature-settings: \"tnum\"` on every money / numeric cell."
    - "Apply `font-feature-settings: \"ss01\"` globally on the body element."
    - Pair every feature explanation with a composited product UI mockup; the brand's argument is "look at the actual product."
  never:
    - generic purple-on-white AI chrome unrelated to this brand
    - dropping DESIGN.md component variants or rationale during restyle
    - bump display weight above 300 — at 400 the brand's editorial air collapses.
    - add new accent colors outside the documented gradient stops (cream / orange / lavender / indigo / ruby / magenta).
    - "use the indigo `{tokens.color.primary}` as a body-text color \u2014 it's a CTA and link color, not a type color at body size."
    - "shrink button padding below `8px 16px` \u2014 the tight pill is part of the brand's transactional feel."
    - "render money cells without `tnum` \u2014 it breaks the quiet financial-data signature."
    - replace the pill shape with rounded-rectangles for buttons.

examples:
  good:
    - ref: https://stripe.com
      note: Live brand marketing / product surfaces
    - ref: https://getdesign.md/stripe/design-md
      note: Source DESIGN.md analysis

